#!/bin/bash
# oneplus-erhai-nautilus postrm: restore Ubuntu's nautilus + gschema and drop
# the diversions on remove/purge.  On upgrade the new version keeps them (its
# postinst has already reinstalled the payload), so nothing is done then.
set -e

BIN=/usr/bin/nautilus
SCHEMA=/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas/org.gnome.nautilus.gschema.xml
SCHEMA_DIR=/usr/share/glib-2.0/schemas
PKG=oneplus-erhai-nautilus

if [ "$1" = "remove" ] || [ "$1" = "purge" ]; then
	pkill -x nautilus >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
	sleep 1

	restore_diverted() {
		local sys="$1"
		local bak="$sys.erhai-orig"
		if [ -f "$bak" ]; then
			cp -a "$bak" "$sys"
		fi
		if dpkg-divert --list "$sys" 2>/dev/null | grep -qF "$sys"; then
			dpkg-divert --package "$PKG" --remove --no-rename "$sys" >/dev/null 2>&1 || \
				dpkg-divert --remove --no-rename "$sys" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
		fi
		rm -f "$bak"
	}

	restore_diverted "$SCHEMA"
	restore_diverted "$BIN"

	if command -v glib-compile-schemas >/dev/null 2>&1; then
		glib-compile-schemas "$SCHEMA_DIR" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
	fi
fi

exit 0
